  <prompt>Expand Spaarke.ArchTests into real fitness functions: "no non-AI code injects AI-internal types" (ADR-013), "no IDataverseService as/is ServiceClient casts outside the shared extension", layer-dependency rules, and God-class LOC/ctor-dep thresholds. PLUS three deployment-refactor rules (accepted 2026-08-13): (a) every customer-critical IOptions&lt;T&gt; registered in DI is [Required]-annotated + ValidateOnStart (enforces #2 / task 061; allowlist = 061's gated-options exemption list), (b) the Graph app-role list has a single source of truth in GraphAppRoles.cs (enforces #4 / task 062), (c) [TRACKING FLAG — report-only until its owning migration lands] the remaining secret-based Dataverse credential path: the shared-lib app-only path (DataverseServiceClientImpl/DataverseWebApiService) is STILL ClientSecretCredential-based (assessment §Addendum 2026-08-13). Author rule (c) as a [Skip]-until reporting rule OWNED BY the NG1 shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration (#3b, decided by task 011's design) — NOT task 060 (which drops only the vestigial separate Dataverse S2S app-reg, no code migration). When #3b lands, rule (c) becomes enforcing: no ClientSecretCredential/AuthType=ClientSecret for Dataverse scopes outside the ADR-028:24 allowlist. Rules (a)/(b) MUST fail on a seeded violation and pass on clean code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with architecture-fitness-test expertise (ArchUnitNET or equivalent). Follow ADR-013 + ADR-010. These rules lock in the R3 remediations so the grade holds.</role>
  <goal>Spaarke.ArchTests carries the new fitness functions; each rule demonstrably fails on a seeded violation and passes on current clean code; build + full test green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-14 / design.md §9. A+ is sustained, not achieved once — convert findings into enforced invariants. These rules make the BFF remediations (facade compliance task 024, downcast consolidation task 021) permanent, plus general layer + God-class guards. Extends the existing Spaarke.ArchTests project (archived-R3 item #8 God-class audit becomes the LOC/ctor-dep threshold rule). EXPANDED 2026-08-13 (deployment-complexity refactor ask, project CLAUDE.md decision): rules (a)/(b)/(c) lock in tasks 061 (uniform config validation — allowlist for kill-switch-gated deferred options comes from 061's exemption list in notes/), 062 (GraphAppRoles.cs single source — rule fails if a second hardcoded Graph app-role list appears in src/ or if the constant is absent while consumers reference it), and the NG1 #3(b) credential migration (rule c — no ClientSecretCredential/AuthType=ClientSecret for Dataverse scopes outside the documented allowlist: SpeAdmin per-tenant, OBO/ConfidentialClient, DataverseAccessDataSource user-context, flag-gated local-dev fallbacks — per ADR-028:24; task 060 does NOT own this, it drops the vestigial app-reg only). Sequencing: rule (a) owner = 061, (b) = 062, (c) = the NG1 #3(b) migration (task 011's design). If an owner has not executed, author its rule against the TARGET state as [Skip]-until-owner-lands with the owning task cited — never water a rule down to pass on the unremediated state.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/**/Spaarke.ArchTests/ (new fitness-function tests + seeded-violation fixtures)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">Extends the existing Spaarke.ArchTests project.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: add fitness functions for (1) no non-AI code injects AI-internal types, (2) no IDataverseService as/is ServiceClient casts outside the shared extension, (3) layer-dependency rules, (4) God-class LOC/ctor-dep thresholds, (5) [rule a] every customer-critical IOptions&lt;T&gt; registered in DI carries [Required] on critical props + ValidateOnStart, exempting only 061's documented gated-options allowlist, (6) [rule b] GraphAppRoles.cs is the only Graph app-role list in src/ (no second hardcoded role-GUID list), (7) [rule c] no ClientSecretCredential / AuthType=ClientSecret construction for Dataverse scopes outside the ADR-028 allowlist (SpeAdmin per-tenant, OBO, DataverseAccessDataSource user-context, flag-gated local-dev fallback). Each rule MUST fail on a seeded violation AND pass on current clean code (or be [Skip]-until its owning task lands — 061 for (a), 062 for (b), the NG1 #3(b) migration for (c) — never weakened to pass dirty state).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: these are fitness tests (KEEP category — architectural invariants), not scaffolding; behavior over mocks.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: extend Spaarke.ArchTests only; do not add a new test project.</constraint>
    <constraint source="net10-2026-08-14">Build on the net10 ArchTests state (handback `notes/r3-handoff.md`): `Spaarke.ArchTests` is GREEN with 28 tests; the ADR-010 1:1-interface ceiling is **153** (re-armed from 76 — legit seams; `IsRecordType` now detects record structs). Your new rules (a/b/c) must coexist — do NOT lower the 153 ceiling or fight the existing rules. The net10 H2 guard test **`DiGraphValidationTests`** (asserts a clean DI graph, `ValidateOnBuild`/`ValidateScopes` on) is MAINTAIN/KEEP — do NOT delete/weaken/duplicate it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Architecture fitness functions</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
