    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (FULL + TEST-MODIFYING reason). Load ADR-013/ADR-010 + TEST-ARCHITECTURE.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the facade rule: no non-AI namespace may reference/inject IActionResolver/IActionRunner/IPlaybookLookupService (ADR-013).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the downcast rule: no IDataverseService as/is ServiceClient cast outside the shared Spaarke.Dataverse extension.</step>
    <step order="3">Add layer-dependency rules and God-class LOC/ctor-dep threshold rules.</step>
    <step order="3a">Add rule (a) IOptions-validated-on-start: enumerate DI-registered options (AddOptions + Configure&lt;&gt;), assert customer-critical ones are [Required]-annotated + ValidateOnStart; consume 061's gated-options exemption list from projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/ as the allowlist (if 061 not yet landed, author against target state + [Skip]-until with owning task cited).</step>
    <step order="3b">Add rule (b) GraphAppRoles single-source: no second hardcoded Graph app-role GUID list in src/; the constant exists once task 062 lands ([Skip]-until if not).</step>
    <step order="3c">Add rule (c) as a [Skip]-until TRACKING flag for the remaining secret-based Dataverse path (shared-lib DataverseServiceClientImpl/DataverseWebApiService per assessment §Addendum 2026-08-13): no ClientSecretCredential/AuthType=ClientSecret for Dataverse scopes outside the ADR-028:24 allowlist. Owner = the NG1 #3(b) migration (task 011's design), NOT task 060. Report-only (Skip) until #3b lands, then flip to enforcing.</step>
    <step order="4">For each rule, add a seeded-violation fixture proving the rule fails, then confirm the rule passes on current clean code (or is [Skip]-until its owning task lands).</step>
    <step order="5">dotnet build + full dotnet test green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 040 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spaarke.ArchTests already exists (R1 forcing-function layer) but lacks the facade / downcast / layer / God-class rules.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this extends the existing ArchTests project with new rules; no new test project is created.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without these fitness functions, the R3 remediations (facade compliance, downcast collapse) silently re-drift as the codebase grows — exactly the grade-drift that made R3 necessary.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/**/Spaarke.ArchTests/ (new fitness functions + seeded-violation fixtures)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each new rule, it FAILS on its seeded violation and PASSES on current clean code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the suite, dotnet build + full dotnet test are green with the new rules active.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no new test project was created (Spaarke.ArchTests extended in place).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rules (a)/(b)/(c) exist: (a) a seeded DI-registered customer-critical options class WITHOUT ValidateOnStart fails the rule while 061's exempted gated options do not; (b) a seeded second hardcoded Graph app-role GUID list fails the rule; (c) rule (c) exists as a [Skip]-until tracking flag that detects a seeded ClientSecretCredential-for-Dataverse outside the ADR-028 allowlist; it stays report-only until the NG1 #3(b) migration (task 011's design) lands, then flips to enforcing — owner is the NG1 migration, not task 060.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no rule was weakened/tuned to pass on unremediated state — any rule whose owning task (060/061/062) has not landed is [Skip]-until with the owning task cited, not deleted or diluted.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-14 / design.md §9 + archived-R3 item #8. Gate for task 042 (CI wiring). EXPANDED 2026-08-13: rule (a) enforces task 061 (#2), rule (b) enforces task 062 (#4), rule (c) is a report-only tracking flag for the remaining secret-based Dataverse path owned by the NG1 #3(b) migration (task 011's design) — task 060 is the #3a vestigial-app-reg drop only. Per the accepted r1 ask (notes/deployment-refactors-assessment-2026-08-12.md §3 + §Addendum 2026-08-13).</notes>

